    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0772" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg712"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Sir
                            Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 21st instant, accompanied by an approved minute of
                    the privy council in reference to the discriminating tax of $1 levied upon
                    American vessels entering or clearing from Canadian ports.</p>
                <p>A copy of this correspondence has been transmitted to the Secretary of the
                    Treasury, to whom I shall also be glad to forward, upon its receipt, a copy of
                    your promised further note in reply to mine of the 31st ultimo upon that
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
